  "text": "I'll start by reading the ego-browser skill and the approved input, then open ChatGPT in a dedicated task space for this transport run.Skill is loaded. Next I’ll inspect the approved input and the job directory, then open ChatGPT in a unique task space.I’ll open a unique task space and inspect ChatGPT’s UI, including how file upload works.Task space 16 is ready. Next I’ll inspect helper usage and open ChatGPT.ChatGPT is open. I’ll wait for the UI to settle, then inspect the visible controls.Logged in as Pro. I’ll open the model picker next and choose the highest reasoning mode that’s actually shown.The picker is open. I’ll inspect the screenshot and then choose the highest reasoning option that’s actually listed.The picker already shows 6 Pro. I’ll open the full model list and read the slider so I can confirm the highest reasoning setting.Highest mode is already **6 Pro** (slider 4/4). I’ll keep that, upload `input.md`, and send the Korean request once.I’ll use the composer’s add-file control and attach `input.md` through the visible upload path.The add-files menu is open. I’ll attach `input.md` through the computer-upload option.The attachment is on the composer. I’ll add the Korean instruction, send once, then write the submitted receipt immediately.The prompt and attachment are in the composer. I’ll confirm the full text, send once, then write the submitted receipt.The send didn’t go out because of a module-format error. I’ll switch to ESM imports and send once.The composer lookup missed the actual editor node. I’ll inspect the live DOM and restore the prompt if it was lost.The prompt is still in the editor. I’ll send it once and write the submitted receipt.The request is in. ChatGPT is thinking in 6 Pro, so I’ll wait and poll instead of sending again.The conversation URL is now stable. I’ll update the receipt and keep polling while it continues generating.It’s still thinking in Pro mode. I’ll keep polling and won’t treat a partial answer as complete.S